<code>assert index >= 0 && index <= \old(this.size()) && role != null => \forall int i; index <= i && i < \old(this.size()); (this.get(i).equals(\old(this.get(i+1))) || (\old(this.get(i+1)) == null && this.get(i) == null));</code>

Explanation:
- The condition `index >= 0 && index <= \old(this.size())` ensures that the index is within the valid range.
- The condition `role != null` ensures that the role being added is not null.
- The quantifier `\forall int i; index <= i && i < \old(this.size());` iterates over all valid indices starting from the insertion point to the old size of the list.
- Inside the quantifier, `(this.get(i).equals(\old(this.get(i+1))) || (\old(this.get(i+1)) == null && this.get(i) == null))` checks that each element at the current position is either equal to the old element at the next position or both are null (to handle cases where the old element might have been null).
